{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): mrs callahan, come through. i'll grab a blood pressure, the doctor's still fighting the computer.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): ok. um, sorry, i'm a bit all over the place this morning.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): you're alright. one eighteen over seventy four, pulse 86. he'll call you in a tick.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): hi. sorry, the screen just froze. what brings you in?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): i'm pregnant, and my husband got told at a screening camp he's got the thalassaemia trait. i'm really scared for the baby.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): say that again? i was on the wrong tab.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): err, dave, my husband. thalassaemia trait, from that camp. i'm sixteen weeks. i just, i need to know about the baby.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): sixteen weeks. and you've got asthma on here. still a problem?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): yeah, since i was little. it hasn't gone.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): what do you actually take? the meds list hasn't loaded.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): umm, the brown puffer. fluticazone, two puffs twice a day. and ventolin, salbutamol, only when i get tight.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): anything the midwife started?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): folic acid, 500 micrograms, once a day. my sister's on biotin for her hair, she wants me on it, but i've never taken that.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): that's your sister's, not yours. dave on tablets, or is that his own business?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): he's on metforman for his sugar. that's his diabetes, not mine. i don't take it.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): right, his metforman. any chest pain?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): any fever?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): never.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): spotting or bleeding?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): not really.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): dizziness?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): not that either.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): and the asthma, any wheeze at night?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): no... well, sometimes. mainly if the neighbour's cat's been on the couch.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): headaches?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): mm, i suppose. sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): was that a yes? the cursor jumped. say it again.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): uh, i don't know. maybe. not a proper headache.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): too vague, i'll leave it. chest is clear, no wheeze just now. tummy's soft, not tender.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): so if dave's a carrier does the baby definitely get sick? i was up at two reading all this stuff.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): not definitely. you both have to carry the trait. my working impression is the risk to this baby hangs on your result, not on his alone.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): if i am a carrier, what's the chance? and is sixteen weeks too late?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): one in four for the major form if you're both carriers. sixteen weeks isn't too late. we'll do the bloods.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): which ones? they don't go near the baby, do they? i had a coffee, is fasting a thing?",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): no fasting, coffee's fine. full blood count and haemoglobin electrophoresis, your blood only. i'm ordering both.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): and genetic counselling, the pamphlet said to ask. can we see them today?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): not today. if the electrophoresis comes back that you're a carrier too, then i'll refer you and dave for genetic counselling.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): do i come back even if it's fine? i can't just sit on it.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (DOCTOR): either way i'll see you in a fortnight with the results. keep the fluticazone and the ventolin, and don't start that biotin.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): i can book the blood test and a review for a fortnight. thursday arvo ok?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): thursday's good. thanks. sorry, i know that was a lot of questions."
 ],
